# ArgusOps Engineering & UI Design Standards

ArgusOps v1.1 is an intelligent AI Agent Cluster Management, Orchestration, and Cost-Optimization Platform designed for enterprise cloud swarms and local PC multi-agent environments (Claude, Antigravity, and Hermes).

Every component, route, service, and script in this codebase MUST strictly comply with these rules.

---

## 1. Visual & Design System Standards

### 1.1 Enterprise SaaS Aesthetic
- **Light-Mode Foundation**: ArgusOps enforces a clean, high-trust, light-mode enterprise SaaS aesthetic.
- **Core Color Tokens**:
  - Main App / Canvas Canvas: `bg-slate-50`
  - Cards, Modals & Surface Panels: `bg-white`
  - Structural Borders & Separators: `border-slate-200`
  - Primary Typography: `text-slate-900`
  - Secondary & Supporting Text: `text-slate-500`
  - Muted Text & Icons: `text-slate-400`
  - Subtle Surface Hovers: `hover:bg-slate-100` / `hover:border-slate-300`

### 1.2 Status Badge Color Tokens
Agent lifecycle and system status badges must use these exact utility combinations across all dashboard, cluster, and log tables:
- **ACTIVE**: Emerald
  - Badge: `bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-700 border-emerald-200`
  - Pulse / Status Dot: `bg-emerald-500`
  - State: Agent actively processing assigned sub-tasks within allocated quota.
- **HIBERNATED (Zero-Token)**: Slate
  - Badge: `bg-slate-100 text-slate-600 border-slate-200`
  - Status Dot: `bg-slate-400`
  - State: Standby agent suspended by Master Hypervisor to prevent over-provisioning token burn.
- **PAUSED_NUDGE**: Amber
  - Badge: `bg-amber-50 text-amber-700 border-amber-200`
  - Status Dot: `bg-amber-500`
  - State: Agent temporarily paused for human-in-the-loop review, clarification, or retry approval.
- **KILLED_LOOP**: Rose
  - Badge: `bg-rose-50 text-rose-700 border-rose-200`
  - Status Dot: `bg-rose-500`
  - State: Circuit breaker triggered; rogue agent terminated due to repetitive error loops or runaway RAM/token drain.

### 1.3 Strict Dashboard Shell Geometry
To prevent layout clipping, unexpected horizontal scrolling, or broken viewport responsiveness:
- **Root Shell Container**: `flex h-screen w-screen overflow-hidden bg-slate-50`
- **Fixed Left Sidebar**: `w-64 shrink-0 border-r border-slate-200 bg-white flex flex-col`
- **Sticky Top Header**: `h-16 shrink-0 sticky top-0 z-30 bg-white border-b border-slate-200 flex items-center justify-between px-6`
- **Main Content Area**: `flex-1 min-w-0 overflow-y-auto overflow-x-hidden p-6 space-y-6`
- **Safety Rule**: Every flex child containing tables, pre/code blocks, or long metric strings must include `min-w-0` to maintain strict boundary constraints.

