## 2. Engineering & Architecture Standards

### 2.1 Technology Stack & Conventions
- **Framework**: Next.js App Router (TypeScript, React 19).
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS v4, utilizing `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for conditional class joining.
- **Database**: SQLite with Prisma ORM (`file:./dev.db`).
- **Icons**: `lucide-react` for clean, professional enterprise iconography.
- **Formatters**: Use centralized utility functions (`formatTokens`, `formatCurrency`) in `src/lib/utils.ts` for all financial and token representations.

### 2.2 Local PC Background Daemon (<150MB RAM)
- Daemon code resides in `/daemon`.
- Must run as an ultra-lightweight background process consuming `<150MB RAM`.
- Provides low-latency interception (`<100ms`) of local agent tool calls and file lock synchronization across Claude, Antigravity, and Hermes.

### 2.3 Implementation & Quality Assurance
- **Zero TODO Policy**: No placeholder comments (`// TODO`, `// FIXME`) or incomplete mock stubs. All implemented interfaces, forms, and services must be fully functional and robust.
- **Defensive Error Handling**: All API routes, background workers, and UI forms must implement explicit validation and actionable error states.

